From: Reefy maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Keep backup GPT writes durable before replacing primary metadata

GPTData::SaveGPTData writes the backup table/header before the primary copy.
Use synchronous writes so a process interruption cannot leave an unflushed
backup while the primary metadata is replaced. In particular, boot-disk
relocation must retain a usable copy if its bounded command is terminated.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/diskio-unix.cc
+++ b/diskio-unix.cc
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@ int DiskIO::OpenForWrite(void) {
    Close();
 
    // try to open the device; may fail....
-   fd = open(realFilename.c_str(), O_WRONLY | O_CREAT, S_IWUSR | S_IRUSR | S_IRGRP | S_IROTH);
+   fd = open(realFilename.c_str(), O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_SYNC, S_IWUSR | S_IRUSR | S_IRGRP | S_IROTH);
 #ifdef __APPLE__
    // MacOS X requires a shared lock under some circumstances....
    if (fd < 0) {
